From 4cb4701e1029970f17b39f57d1fd436d668977a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonardo Grasso <me@leonardograsso.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:54:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(mermaid-text): fit sequence diagrams to the width budget

Sequence diagrams ignored render_with_width / RenderOptions::max_width.
Over budget, cap label-driven participant gaps at a shared level and wrap
message labels to the room their arrow gets; further attempts reduce the
participant box padding and wrap participant labels. Notes and self-message
labels wrap to fit, and event rows grow per wrapped line. Participant names
and note words stay whole whenever an attempt fits that way; only otherwise
are they split. Among the fitting attempts of that kind the fewest rows win;
otherwise the narrowest is returned. An attempt that block frames or notes
push past the budget is planned again for the overshoot.
Unbudgeted or already-fitting renders are byte-identical.
