 This project adheres to [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/).
 
+## Unreleased
+
+### Added
+
+- Sequence diagrams honour `render_with_width` / `RenderOptions::max_width`
+  (they previously ignored it). Over budget, label-driven gaps are capped at a
+  shared level and message labels wrap to the room their arrow gets; further
+  attempts reduce participant box padding and wrap participant labels. Notes
+  and self-message labels wrap to fit, and rows grow for wrapped lines.
+  Participant names and note words are kept whole whenever any attempt fits
+  that way, and only otherwise split; among the fitting attempts of that kind
+  the one with the fewest rows wins. An attempt that block frames or notes
+  push past the budget is planned again for the overshoot. Renders without a
+  budget, or that already fit, are byte-identical to before.
+
+### Changed
+
+- `tests/strict_max_width.rs` uses a class diagram as its fixed-width
+  fixture, since sequence diagrams now fit the budget.
+
